1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,920
Now, assembled gods and goddesses, may I have your attention, please?

2
00:00:11,140 --> 00:00:14,600
The difficulty level for this next salvation will be the dreaded us class.

3
00:00:14,940 --> 00:00:17,260
And doing the honors this time will be...

4
00:00:17,260 --> 00:00:21,420
The goddess Ristante.

5
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:24,280
I'm so glad it's you, Lista.

6
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:26,080
You have some big tasks ahead of you.

7
00:00:26,080 --> 00:00:29,320
Once you finish this, you'll be a full-fledged, legitimate goddess.

8
00:00:29,320 --> 00:00:30,440
Thank you all.

9
00:00:30,820 --> 00:00:35,920
I vow to use this endeavor to better myself and gain experience so I can one day become a high-rinking goddess.

10
00:00:36,380 --> 00:00:38,520
Are you freaking kidding me?

11
00:00:44,080 --> 00:00:47,180
I can't believe they gave me an S-class job.

12
00:00:47,860 --> 00:00:49,860
I'm Ristante, or Rista for short.

13
00:00:50,320 --> 00:00:54,720
I was born into the unified divine realm, let's just say, 100 years ago.

14
00:00:54,720 --> 00:01:00,280
I've summoned heroes from the human realm to save worlds on the brink of collapse five times so far.

15
00:01:01,320 --> 00:01:06,240
But compared to the higher-level gods and goddesses, five times is nothing to brag about.

16
00:01:06,640 --> 00:01:11,820
The average is about 10, and some of the big-deal deities have saved hundreds of worlds.

17
00:01:11,820 --> 00:01:20,520
And in case you're wondering, S-class means that the world is so messed up and dangerous that even the most experienced gods don't want to go near it.

18
00:01:20,520 --> 00:01:32,200
The last few times, I've chosen a young man from Japan to summon as the hero.

19
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:33,760
They seem the easiest to train.

20
00:01:34,300 --> 00:01:40,200
Japan has a lot of stories about people being taken to another world for various reasons, so they get the idea pretty quickly.

21
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:46,800
And though the public is on the verge of being completely oversaturated with this kind of story, the sheer number of them can only mean it's still popular.

22
00:01:47,060 --> 00:01:48,580
Wait, why am I narrating?

23
00:01:49,620 --> 00:01:51,760
I'm so stressed, I'm losing my mind.

24
00:01:52,320 --> 00:01:55,540
I can only summon one hero, so I have to choose carefully.

25
00:01:57,120 --> 00:01:59,340
Suzuki, Sasaki.

26
00:02:00,280 --> 00:02:01,940
Suzuki, Yamada.

27
00:02:02,740 --> 00:02:03,940
Sasaki, Sato.

28
00:02:04,400 --> 00:02:06,320
Suzuki, Tanaka, Sasaki, Yamada.

29
00:02:06,540 --> 00:02:07,840
Sasaki, Suzuki, Yamada, Yamada.

30
00:02:07,920 --> 00:02:09,060
Tanaka, Yamada, Sasaki, Suzuki.

31
00:02:09,060 --> 00:02:12,600
Oh, jeez, they owe the light to me.

32
00:02:15,340 --> 00:02:18,140
I need to make some kind of decision here.

33
00:02:31,760 --> 00:02:32,740
Stupid paperwork.

34
00:02:33,420 --> 00:02:35,800
