257
00:12:40,880 --> 00:12:43,880
It's never gonna ring

258
00:12:43,880 --> 00:12:46,880
I'll have to wait forever

259
00:12:49,880 --> 00:12:50,880
You ring!

260
00:12:54,880 --> 00:12:58,880
Sexy, so fresh and so clean

261
00:12:58,880 --> 00:13:00,880
I remember telling you to knock first

262
00:13:00,880 --> 00:13:01,880
Yeah, I'm the rude one here

263
00:13:01,880 --> 00:13:03,880
So how's the training going?

264
00:13:03,880 --> 00:13:04,880
Status

265
00:13:08,880 --> 00:13:11,880
You leveled up like crazy just from working out?

266
00:13:11,880 --> 00:13:14,880
You do have that unique XP boost skill after all

267
00:13:14,880 --> 00:13:16,880
I know you have other special skills

268
00:13:16,880 --> 00:13:19,880
If it were completely up to me, I'd like to max out my levels first

269
00:13:19,880 --> 00:13:21,880
You'd spend the rest of your life in here!

270
00:13:21,880 --> 00:13:24,880
Time passes slowly in this realm, but we don't have forever

271
00:13:24,880 --> 00:13:26,880
We have to get going

272
00:13:27,880 --> 00:13:28,880
On to Gaia Brande!

273
00:13:28,880 --> 00:13:29,880
Yeah, okay

274
00:13:32,880 --> 00:13:33,880
I am perfectly prepared

275
00:13:34,880 --> 00:13:36,880
I am 100% ready for this

276
00:13:36,880 --> 00:13:37,880
What is he doing?

277
00:13:37,880 --> 00:13:39,880
Trying to work in some cool little catchphrase?

278
00:13:39,880 --> 00:13:40,880
Great!

279
00:13:40,880 --> 00:13:41,880
But you don't have to say that

280
00:13:41,880 --> 00:13:43,880
Let's just go already!

281
00:13:43,880 --> 00:13:54,880
The great goddess Ishtar determined this was the perfect place for us to enter this world

282
00:13:55,880 --> 00:13:58,880
Now, we need to go into the town of Idona and get your equipment

283
00:13:58,880 --> 00:14:13,880
Hello! You just passing through?

284
00:14:13,880 --> 00:14:15,880
Hello! Yes we are!

285
00:14:15,880 --> 00:14:20,880
Are you sure it's safe to be casually walking around this strange village when you're dressed like a stripper?

286
00:14:20,880 --> 00:14:22,880
Watch your mouth, pal!

287
00:14:22,880 --> 00:14:25,880
And I use my goddess power to make it look like I'm wearing normal clothes

288
00:14:25,880 --> 00:14:29,880
I'm not nearly as concerned about your outfit as I am about that man

289
00:14:29,880 --> 00:14:31,880
He could well be a monster in disguise

290
00:14:31,880 --> 00:14:33,880
Jeez, he's just a regular guy

291
00:14:33,880 --> 00:14:35,880
I don't like the look of him

292
00:14:35,880 --> 00:14:37,880
It's possible he's a shapeshifter

293
00:14:37,880 --> 00:14:38,880
No, it's not

294
00:14:38,880 --> 00:14:42,880
Even if he's not literally a monster, he could be a thief or a mass murderer

295
00:14:42,880 --> 00:14:45,880
I may need to take him out before he kills us

296
00:14:45,880 --> 00:14:49,880
You're the one who sounds like a murderer, you paranoid weirdo!

297
00:14:49,880 --> 00:14:52,880
Oh wow, you sure look super pretty in that outfit, lady

298
00:14:52,880 --> 00:14:54,880
You're like a goddess or something

299
00:14:54,880 --> 00:14:56,880
How sweet!

300
00:14:56,880 --> 00:14:59,880
And I said little children can always recognize true beauty

301
00:14:59,880 --> 00:15:03,880
Mister, you got some funny clothes but you seem really cool anyway

302
00:15:03,880 --> 00:15:07,880
My, are you gonna let some childish remark upset you?

303
00:15:07,880 --> 00:15:09,880
I bet they call you Mister Cool

304
00:15:09,880 --> 00:15:11,880
What's your real name?

305
00:15:11,880 --> 00:15:13,880
It's Saya

306
00:15:13,880 --> 00:15:16,880
Oh, my name's Nina, nice to meet you

307
00:15:16,880 --> 00:15:19,880
I'd love to watch this interaction go on but we have a job to do

308
00:15:19,880 --> 00:15:23,880
Oh tell me, Nina, is there a blacksmith or weapon shop nearby?

309
00:15:23,880 --> 00:15:25,880
Yeah, there's a place like that real close

310
00:15:25,880 --> 00:15:28,880
Just a little bit down the road that way

311
00:15:28,880 --> 00:15:31,880
Thanks Nina, I appreciate it

312
00:15:31,880 --> 00:15:33,880
Here's a little present from me to you

313
00:15:33,880 --> 00:15:37,880
This should be more than enough money to buy whatever you think you're gonna need

314
00:15:39,880 --> 00:15:40,880
Welcome

315
00:15:43,880 --> 00:15:45,880
Definitely gonna take this steel armor right here

316
00:15:45,880 --> 00:15:47,880
Nice, excellent choice

317
00:15:47,880 --> 00:15:48,880
Three sets

318
00:15:48,880 --> 00:15:49,880
Not so fast!

319
00:15:49,880 --> 00:15:51,880
You don't need that much armor!

320
00:15:51,880 --> 00:15:56,880
I do because I need one to wear, one for spare, and one more in case the spare needs a spare

321
00:15:56,880 --> 00:15:58,880
Do you have an armor fetish?

322
00:15:58,880 --> 00:16:02,880
What kind of ridiculous hero spends all his money on three identical sets of armor?

323
00:16:02,880 --> 00:16:04,880
I'll choose one for you, so just stay put, okay?

324
00:16:04,880 --> 00:16:06,880
You're not the boss of me

325
00:16:06,880 --> 00:16:09,880
He's not just cautious, he's pathological

326
00:16:15,880 --> 00:16:17,880
Mmm, that's way better

327
00:16:17,880 --> 00:16:19,880
You really look like the ideal hero to me

328
00:16:21,880 --> 00:16:25,880
I need 30 smoke bombs, 50 medicinal herbs, and 50 anecdotal herbs

329
00:16:25,880 --> 00:16:28,880
Oh, yes, coming right up, sir

330
00:16:28,880 --> 00:16:29,880
Thank you

331
00:16:29,880 --> 00:16:31,880
At least they're not that expensive

332
00:16:31,880 --> 00:16:33,880
But still, you bought so many

333
00:16:33,880 --> 00:16:35,880
There's no telling what we might encounter

334
00:16:35,880 --> 00:16:37,880
So I need to be prepared

335
00:16:37,880 --> 00:16:40,880
I may not look it, but I am a veteran at this stuff

336
00:16:40,880 --> 00:16:43,880
Therefore, I located the perfect starting place for you

337
00:16:43,880 --> 00:16:46,880
There's nothing but weak monsters around here

338
00:16:46,880 --> 00:16:50,880
I'm not so sure, and I highly doubt you're a veteran like you claim

339
00:16:50,880 --> 00:16:52,880
Why would I be lying?

340
00:16:52,880 --> 00:16:53,880
She's right

341
00:16:53,880 --> 00:16:54,880
It's true

342
00:16:54,880 --> 00:16:58,880
Even I can walk over to the next town with no problem at all

343
00:16:58,880 --> 00:17:01,880
Only things we gotta deal with are wibbly wobbly little slimes

344
00:17:01,880 --> 00:17:04,880
If a cute little girl can handle it, then so can you

345
00:17:04,880 --> 00:17:06,880
Does that put your mind at ease?

346
00:17:06,880 --> 00:17:08,880
You look pretty strong, Mr. Seiya

347
00:17:08,880 --> 00:17:10,880
Are you really afraid of going outside of town?

348
00:17:10,880 --> 00:17:14,880
Yeah, underneath all that armor, he's actually just a big, strong, fraidy cat

349
00:17:14,880 --> 00:17:15,880
Well then, take this

350
00:17:15,880 --> 00:17:18,880
This charm will ward off any evil

351
00:17:21,880 --> 00:17:23,880
You didn't put a curse on this, did you?

352
00:17:23,880 --> 00:17:25,880
Jeez! Just stop it!

353
00:17:25,880 --> 00:17:26,880
What'd you say?

354
00:17:26,880 --> 00:17:28,880
Don't pay any attention to him, he's just a little sick

355
00:17:28,880 --> 00:17:30,880
Nina, what have you got into?

356
00:17:30,880 --> 00:17:32,880
Hey, Papa!

357
00:17:32,880 --> 00:17:35,880
I apologize, my daughter can be a little nosy

358
00:17:35,880 --> 00:17:36,880
I'm sorry if she bothered you

359
00:17:36,880 --> 00:17:38,880
No, no, not at all

360
00:17:38,880 --> 00:17:39,880
Right?

361
00:17:39,880 --> 00:17:42,880
No, not very much at least

362
00:17:42,880 --> 00:17:45,880
Hmm, so he's not completely disagreeable

363
00:17:45,880 --> 00:17:48,880
Okay, it's finally monster fight o'clock!

364
00:17:48,880 --> 00:17:52,880
I don't see any good reason why we need to go out looking for trouble

365
00:17:52,880 --> 00:17:54,880
Don't be such a diaper baby!

366
00:17:54,880 --> 00:17:56,880
You have enough gear to take on an army!

367
00:17:58,880 --> 00:18:00,880
There's a little monster!

368
00:18:00,880 --> 00:18:02,880
I've never seen anything like that before

369
00:18:02,880 --> 00:18:04,880
Are they genetically engineered?

370
00:18:04,880 --> 00:18:06,880
Don't you know what a slime is?

371
00:18:06,880 --> 00:18:07,880
These things are in like every game

372
00:18:07,880 --> 00:18:08,880
Nope

373
00:18:08,880 --> 00:18:10,880
You are really Japanese, right?

374
00:18:10,880 --> 00:18:12,880
Slimes jump at you when they attack

375
00:18:12,880 --> 00:18:15,880
But they're so weak that practically anyone can kill them with just a stick!

376
00:18:15,880 --> 00:18:16,880
So...

377
00:18:20,880 --> 00:18:21,880
Hey!

378
00:18:21,880 --> 00:18:22,880
What are you doing?

379
00:18:22,880 --> 00:18:23,880
What are you doing?

380
00:18:23,880 --> 00:18:24,880
Ah!

381
00:18:24,880 --> 00:18:25,880
Now!

382
00:18:25,880 --> 00:18:26,880
Atomic Split Slash!

383
00:18:37,880 --> 00:18:38,880
Overkill much?

384
00:18:38,880 --> 00:18:39,880
It's just the slime!

385
00:18:39,880 --> 00:18:41,880
They're like the easiest thing to beat!

386
00:18:41,880 --> 00:18:42,880
I'm not done!

387
00:18:42,880 --> 00:18:44,880
I'm afraid it may still be alive!

388
00:18:44,880 --> 00:18:46,880
Casting Hell's Fire!

389
00:18:48,880 --> 00:18:51,880
The slime has gone okay so just cut it out!

390
00:18:51,880 --> 00:18:52,880
No, not yet.

391
00:18:52,880 --> 00:18:54,880
There could still be danger

392
00:18:54,880 --> 00:18:55,880
Huh?

393
00:18:55,880 --> 00:18:58,880
You mean you know more than two special attacks already?

394
00:18:58,880 --> 00:19:01,880
How about another Atomic Split Slash attack?

395
00:19:02,880 --> 00:19:05,880
Why use the same attack twice in a row like that?

396
00:19:05,880 --> 00:19:06,880
Uh-uh!

397
00:19:06,880 --> 00:19:07,880
Have another Hell's Fire!

398
00:19:07,880 --> 00:19:10,880
Of course you'd have to use that one again!

399
00:19:11,880 --> 00:19:13,880
It can't be more dead!

400
00:19:13,880 --> 00:19:14,880
Stop!

401
00:19:14,880 --> 00:19:16,880
We get it!

402
00:19:16,880 --> 00:19:18,880
Atomic Split Slash!

403
00:19:22,880 --> 00:19:23,880
Done.

404
00:19:23,880 --> 00:19:24,880
That was just a slime!

405
00:19:24,880 --> 00:19:27,880
You vaporized it on the first Atomic whatever!

406
00:19:28,880 --> 00:19:29,880
Always be on guard.

407
00:19:29,880 --> 00:19:30,880
No, not always!

408
00:19:31,880 --> 00:19:34,880
Honestly, Seiya, I mean you do already have the scan ability, right?

409
00:19:35,880 --> 00:19:36,880
Use that to check the slime stats!

410
00:19:37,880 --> 00:19:38,880
I did check them, Kay.

411
00:19:40,880 --> 00:19:42,880
Its attack and defense were both in the single digits.

412
00:19:43,880 --> 00:19:44,880
Then why did you throw everything at it?

413
00:19:45,880 --> 00:19:47,880
There could be more to it than just the visible data.

414
00:19:48,880 --> 00:19:49,880
Try to have some more faith in your skills!

415
00:19:49,880 --> 00:19:53,880
Anyway, I hope this boosted your confidence a bit, Seiya.

416
00:19:54,880 --> 00:19:58,880
Look, you have incredible power and all the equipment that you would possibly need, so let's...

417
00:19:59,880 --> 00:20:00,880
Oh, what's that?

418
00:20:01,880 --> 00:20:02,880
Very impressive swordsmanship.

419
00:20:04,880 --> 00:20:05,880
You're the one, right?

420
00:20:06,880 --> 00:20:08,880
Yes, you must be the one.

421
00:20:09,880 --> 00:20:10,880
Wait, who are you?

422
00:20:10,880 --> 00:20:13,880
Pleased to make your acquaintance fair, goddess and brave hero.

423
00:20:13,880 --> 00:20:14,880
Welcome!

424
00:20:14,880 --> 00:20:17,880
I'm one of four heavenly kings serving the demon lord.

425
00:20:17,880 --> 00:20:19,880
I am known as Chaos Machina!

426
00:20:20,880 --> 00:20:21,880
What? No way, you can't be!

427
00:20:22,880 --> 00:20:24,880
We're not supposed to be facing a powerful enemy yet!

428
00:20:25,880 --> 00:20:26,880
You sound quite surprised.

429
00:20:27,880 --> 00:20:32,880
Our wise demon lord detected the signs of a hero's summoning before it even happened.

430
00:20:33,880 --> 00:20:34,880
So comically predictable.

431
00:20:35,880 --> 00:20:40,880
Every time a new hero is summoned, they head to an area full of the weakest monsters to boost their skills.

432
00:20:40,880 --> 00:20:42,880
And when I thought about where that might be...

433
00:20:43,880 --> 00:20:45,880
I knew this was the perfect spot to end you!

434
00:20:46,880 --> 00:20:48,880
Now I see why this is an S-class mission.

435
00:20:49,880 --> 00:20:51,880
I can't use any of my normal strategies.

436
00:20:51,880 --> 00:20:54,880
The demon lord has been vigilantly waiting for a hero to appear.

437
00:20:54,880 --> 00:20:57,880
I didn't think we needed to worry, but here we are.

438
00:20:58,880 --> 00:21:00,880
And now that I look at you...

439
00:21:01,880 --> 00:21:03,880
I can tell you're something special.

440
00:21:04,880 --> 00:21:07,880
Deep within you lies the potential to be an incredibly powerful foe.

441
00:21:08,880 --> 00:21:09,880
It's too bad.

442
00:21:10,880 --> 00:21:11,880
That won't do.

443
00:21:11,880 --> 00:21:12,880
No, no, no, no, no.

444
00:21:13,880 --> 00:21:14,880
It just won't do at all!

445
00:21:15,880 --> 00:21:17,880
I'll have to end you right now!

446
00:21:20,880 --> 00:21:22,880
Oh no! I need to scan her right away!

447
00:21:24,880 --> 00:21:27,880
Why are we going up against someone this powerful in the first stage?

448
00:21:29,880 --> 00:21:30,880
How do we get out of this?

449
00:21:31,880 --> 00:21:34,880
I guess we should try to run as fast as we can, but then what?

450
00:21:35,880 --> 00:21:36,880
What do you think, Seiya?

451
00:21:37,880 --> 00:21:38,880
Huh?

452
00:21:38,880 --> 00:21:39,880
Later!

453
00:21:39,880 --> 00:21:40,880
He lost me!

454
00:21:44,880 --> 00:21:46,880
Hey, sweetie! What's the big idea?

455
00:21:47,880 --> 00:21:50,880
Running away without thinking is the smart thing to do.

456
00:21:51,880 --> 00:21:54,880
Most humans wouldn't be so decisive when faced with danger.

457
00:21:55,880 --> 00:21:57,880
Well, how fascinating.

458
00:21:58,880 --> 00:22:00,880
Yes, what a fascinating hero!

459
00:22:03,880 --> 00:22:04,880
Wait for me!

460
00:22:04,880 --> 00:22:07,880
You'd run away and leave a goddess behind!

461
00:22:07,880 --> 00:22:09,880
AAAAAA!

462
00:22:09,880 --> 00:22:39,860
Let's go!

463
00:22:39,880 --> 00:23:09,860
Let's go!

464
00:23:09,880 --> 00:23:39,860
Let's go!

465
00:23:39,880 --> 00:23:40,140
Let's go!

